#!/bin/bash
# claude-phone: keep a Claude Code Remote Control session alive in tmux on a cluster login node,
# to drive it from the Claude mobile app or claude.ai/code. See .claude/claude-phone.md of the project.
set -euo pipefail

SESSION="claude"
PROJECT_DIR="${CLAUDE_PHONE_DIR:-$HOME/neptune}"
PROJECT_NAME="$(basename "$PROJECT_DIR")"
MODE="${CLAUDE_PHONE_MODE:-acceptEdits}"

# The tmux socket lives in the home directory, named after the node: the cleaning of /tmp can no longer
# make the session unreachable, and the socket files tell on which node a session was started.
SOCKET_DIR="$HOME/.tmux"
SOCKET="$SOCKET_DIR/claude-phone-$(hostname -s).sock"

tm() {
    tmux -S "$SOCKET" "$@"
}

usage() {
    echo "Usage: claude-phone [start|stop|status]"
    echo "  start  (default) Start the Remote Control session in tmux and attach to it."
    echo "  stop             Kill the tmux session."
    echo "  status           Tell whether the session runs on this node."
}

resolve_cli() {
    # Standalone CLI first, otherwise the latest binary bundled with the VSCode extension.
    if command -v claude > /dev/null; then
        command -v claude
        return
    fi
    local bundled
    bundled=$(ls -d "$HOME"/.vscode-server/extensions/anthropic.claude-code-*/resources/native-binary/claude 2> /dev/null | sort -V | tail -n 1 || true)
    if [[ -n "$bundled" ]]; then
        echo "$bundled"
        return
    fi
    echo "claude-phone: Claude Code CLI not found, install it with:" >&2
    echo "  curl -fsSL https://claude.ai/install.sh | bash" >&2
    return 1
}

run_loop() {
    # Runs inside tmux. The first run creates the named session, the next ones reattach to it with -c,
    # which only works within about 4 h, hence at most 480 retries of 30 s.
    local cli=$1 name=$2 mode=$3
    local first=1 failures=0 status
    while (( failures < 480 )); do
        if (( first )); then
            nice -n 10 "$cli" remote-control --name "$name" --permission-mode "$mode" && status=0 || status=$?
        else
            nice -n 10 "$cli" remote-control -c && status=0 || status=$?
        fi
        first=0
        if (( status == 0 || status == 130 )); then
            return
        fi
        failures=$(( failures + 1 ))
        echo "claude remote-control exited with code $status, restarting in 30 s (Ctrl+C to stop)."
        sleep 30
    done
    echo "claude-phone: gave up after $failures failures, run 'claude-phone stop' then 'claude-phone start'."
    sleep infinity
}

start() {
    local cli
    cli=$(resolve_cli)
    if ! tm has-session -t "$SESSION" 2> /dev/null; then
        mkdir -p "$SOCKET_DIR" && chmod 700 "$SOCKET_DIR"
        rm -f "$SOCKET"
        local threads="export OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 MKL_NUM_THREADS=4 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=4 CLAUDE_PHONE=1"
        local call
        call="run_loop $(printf '%q ' "$cli" "$PROJECT_NAME" "$MODE")"
        tm new-session -d -s "$SESSION" -c "$PROJECT_DIR" bash -c "$threads; $(declare -f run_loop); $call"
        echo "Started '$SESSION' on $(hostname -s) in $PROJECT_DIR (mode $MODE)."
    fi
    tm attach -t "$SESSION"
}

stop() {
    if tm has-session -t "$SESSION" 2> /dev/null; then
        tm kill-session -t "$SESSION"
        echo "Stopped '$SESSION' on $(hostname -s)."
    else
        echo "No '$SESSION' session on $(hostname -s)."
        other_nodes
    fi
    rm -f "$SOCKET"
}

status() {
    if tm has-session -t "$SESSION" 2> /dev/null; then
        echo "'$SESSION' is running on $(hostname -s)."
    else
        echo "'$SESSION' is not running on $(hostname -s)."
        other_nodes
    fi
}

other_nodes() {
    # tmux is per node: a session started on another login node can only be reached from that node.
    local socket node
    for socket in "$SOCKET_DIR"/claude-phone-*.sock; do
        [[ -e "$socket" && "$socket" != "$SOCKET" ]] || continue
        node=$(basename "$socket" .sock)
        node=${node#claude-phone-}
        echo "A session was started on $node: run 'ssh $node' then 'claude-phone status' (or stop)."
    done
}

case "${1:-start}" in
    start)          start ;;
    stop)           stop ;;
    status)         status ;;
    -h|--help|help) usage ;;
    *)              usage >&2; exit 2 ;;
esac
